[0.0, "o", "1mGaps\u001b[0m                                                                                                       \u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m                                                                                                            \u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m \u001b[1m \u2022 \u001b[0m\u001b[1mLena Petrov (#1):\u001b[0m                                                                                       \u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m \u001b[1m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u2022 \u001b[0mTypeScript is tied only to the 2014\u20132020 CoreSystems role. Recent use at BrightUI isn't stated.      \u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m \u001b[1m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u2022 \u001b[0mAWS is listed under skills but no project backs it.                                                  \u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m \u001b[1m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u2022 \u001b[0mThe claim \"improved model accuracy by 16 points\" is an ML-style metric. It doesn't fit a full stack  \u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m \u001b[1m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mrole.                                                                                                \u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[3"]
[0.0, "o", "2m\u2502\u001b[0m \u001b[1m \u2022 \u001b[0m\u001b[1mLeila Saab (#2):\u001b[0m                                                                                        \u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m \u001b[1m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u2022 \u001b[0mTypeScript appears only in the 2014\u20132020 CloudNine role.                                             \u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m \u001b[1m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u2022 \u001b[0mGraphQL and AWS are skills-list only.                                                                \u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m \u001b[1m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u2022 \u001b[0m\"Improved model accuracy by 5 points\" looks like ML work, so only one measurable result is relevant. \u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m \u001b[1m \u2022 \u001b[0m\u001b[1mLiam Tanaka (#3):\u001b[0m                                                                                       \u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m \u001b[1m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u2022 \u001b[0mHe has no GraphQL.                                                                                   \u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m \u001b[1m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u2022 \u001b[0mAWS is skills-list only.                                                    "]
[0.0, "o", "                         \u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m \u001b[1m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u2022 \u001b[0mTypeScript is tied only to StreamHub (2021\u20132024). His current Beta Inc role lists only JavaScript,   \u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m \u001b[1m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mReact and Node.js.                                                                                   \u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m                                                                                                            \u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m \u001b[1mTakeaways\u001b[0m                                                                                                  \u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m                                                                                                            \u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m \u001b[1m \u2022 \u001b[0mPetrov and Saab tie at 84 and look nearly identical on paper. Petrov's edge is that React and Node.js   \u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m \u001b[1m   \u001b[0mare tied to his current role and TypeScript, MongoDB and GraphQL to concrete CoreSystems work. Saab's  "]
[0.0, "o", " \u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m \u001b[1m   \u001b[0mnice-to-haves are mostly skills-list only.                                                              \u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m \u001b[1m \u2022 \u001b[0mTanaka scores 6 points lower. He has fewer years (5 vs. 12) and no GraphQL, but he does have 3+ years.  \u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m \u001b[1m \u2022 \u001b[0mAll three have the same open question: is TypeScript still in recent use? I'd check that in screening.  \u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m                                                                                                            \u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m I can generate interview questions or run \u001b[1;36;40mexplain_ranking\u001b[0m on Petrov vs. Saab if you want.                  \u001b[32m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m\u2570\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\ufffd"]
